Let me first just say I was immensely lucky several times. I've only 
been playing NetHack since June, so I can't believe I've got my own 
demigod already!

I don't have the dump patch so I don't have a nice, pretty full printout 
of everything. I'll just sum up the major points. A little preface, I'm 
as spoiled as I can get, including poking around the source (most often 
to check the meaning of a message I got). I used every tactic I could 
think of to help my ascension. This entire game took me about 3 or 4 
days, and I don't remember the beginning too accurately. After all, why 
take notes on what happened? The odds of ascending were so poor...

Moron was originally a lawful, female dwarven Valk. Relatively early on 
(before clvl 10) he was trying on uncursed amulets and had a sudden 
gender change. His name is my attempt of reverse psychology on the RNG, 
and also it makes entering stores humorous.

Decided to do Sokoban first. On the way there, I encountered three large 
delicatessans, and no other stores. One of the big reasons I do Sokoban 
first is so I don't have food supply problems in the mines (since I 
won't be killing those tasty Gnomes). I went ahead anyway because I like 
solving the Sokoban puzzles (I never can remember the solutions 
completely, so I always get to solve them anew).

There was a bones file at the Oracle (dLvl 6 or 7) with an astonishing 
wand of wishing (0:2) in it! I got some GDSM with the wand after I 
checked Sokoban ("oR, it cost me a few luck points), went ahead and got 
the bag of holding and a shiny new Grayswandir. I also got boots of 
speed and gauntlets of power to round out my kit.

On the way to minetown I hit another tasty bones file. It had a 
remarkably uncursed bag of holding, a cloak of magic resistance, and a 
few other trivial things. If I'd found that cloak before I got my GDSM I 
probably would've gone with SDSM.

Minetown itself had a disappointing selection of shops. There was a tiny 
rare bookstore with 5 books, one of which was plain. No magic lamps. My 
pets were very well trained at this point thanks to a plethora of tripe 
rations from the food stores, so I went ahead and cleaned out all the 
stores. Got a towel and a stethoscope which came in handy shortly.

I went to Mines End for the luckstone. Mimic of the Mines, same as my 
last 4 or 5 games. Along with the luckstone, I found a touchstone but 
had no way to bless it yet. Back at minetown, I murdered the priestess 
(I had a magic whistle, but no polytraps were found yet) and lost my 
telepathy to the guards. I converted the altar and made some holy water, 
blessed my touchstone, IDed gems, and threw them at a unicorn to make up 
for Sokoban.

I joyously discovered a brown pudding in minetown and quickly proceded 
to carpet the ground with them. By this time I had teleportitis and 
telecontrol intrinsics, so they weren't a problem blocking my way. I had 
a grand ol' sacfest netting me a very large number of spellbooks (I 
probably had 30 by this point, many repeats) as well as several 
artifacts that did me no good since I had Grayswandir. I unfortunately 
managed to get crowned despite dropping my luckstone so it took a while 
before I was content. I also collected a great many items including 
another bag of holding and two plain sacks (which I use for /oCancel). 
Also found some more speed boots. Curse my impatience with wishing...

At this point I was level 14-ish. I had the Identify spell (and many 
others I could barely cast), a robe, no nice helm, but otherwise a 
complete set of armor and weapons. I had my Grayswandir plus another 
silver saber and 25 daggers. I had polymorph and polycontrol rings, so I 
got searching, regen, and warning intrinsics. I also had a tinning 
kit... time for the quest.

Not really much to say about this. I'd played the valk quest before so 
nothing new. By the time I emerged I had about 15 tins of giant meat. 
When I finally ate them all, my strength hit 18/** (I had the gauntlets 
on all the time anyway, but I still like to get my strength up).

Medusa was trivial. I had a ring of levitation and had already genocided 
all ;. After discovering the island, I went back up and fell through a 
trapdoor past it. So I was careful to be blindfolded before going up the 
stairs. I had reflection and I think that would've saved me even without 
the blindfold, but I've never been clear on that. Why risk it? Perseus 
had the boots and shield, neither of which was useful to me. I met my 
first mind flayer (killed from a great distance) and found a wand of 
polymorph!

I polypiled all my duplicate spellbooks and useless potions and scrolls. 
  By the time I was done, stats were maxed and I had most spells. Still 
no charm monster or magic mapping though.

Not much else to say, really. I had the tune to the castle, but went 
around the back anyway. The wand gave me a helm of brilliance (I found 
another in the valley of the dead right afterwards...) and two magic 
markers. I also wished for figurines of a Ki-Rin (as a steed, they're 
awesome) and an archon because I didn't really have anything else I 
needed. The archon got eaten by a purple worm before even leaving the 
level, but the Ki-Rin served me well for a long time. My final wish was 
spent on a much-desired blessed spellbook of charm monster.

So far I'd encountered exactly one altar besides the VotD and Minetown, 
at dlvl 17 with my one and only stash. The only living priest was 
Moloch's in the VotD and I'd saved 60,000 for some protection (I'd 
gotten 4 points from the minetown priest already) but one of my pets 
killed him before I could pay. Grr... Oh well, AC at -37 anyway thanks 
to good luck getting +5s on my armor.

Gehennom was nothing. Found 2 magic lamps, blessed 'em and used as 
light. Orcus's wand of death was the first I'd found, but I found 
another before hitting the wizard. Magic mapping and Detect Treasure got 
me through. In the sanctum, a well-saved scroll of taming while confused 
got me an army of my own, and combined with a wand of secret door 
detection and some cursed pots of gain level, I was in and out in no 
time. No Wizard, even!

The way out was a pain. I ran (rode, really. Had a J steed) through lvls 
30-36 at least 5 times EACH. I liberally used my 12 scrolls of 
teleportation to help me out, but the levels looked like swiss cheese by 
the time I was through with my pickaxe. After the castle, nothing 
happened. I made it without incident to dlvl 1 (quick stop at my stash 
to rebless everything) and picked up the "End Game Bag of Holding" that 
I'd left there earlier. It had wands of teleport, food, pots of full 
healing, and scrolls of gold detection. I dropped everything I didn't 
need and went to the Planes of Earth.

Earth was easy. Rodney fell to my /oDeath quickly and my /oDigging got 
me to the portal in no time. On the planes of Air, I lost my faithful 
Jabberwocky, the only remaining pet I'd had. No big deal, just now I had 
to put on my "oLevitation. Off came slow digest. Air was not hard 
otherwise, conflict helped. On the planes of fire, I used a blindfold 
just so I wouldn't have to keep watching them step on traps, and flew 
straight for the portal. Another no problem. Water was more floating 
around, looking for the portal bubble. The elementals and snakes could 
barely scratch me.

I remembered to remove conflict before entering the Astral Plane. I 
#rubbed one of my lamps for a rubber chicken, so the folks there were no 
sweat. Pestilence first, to the left. I'd never fought the riders before 
and I knew many an adventurer fell to them, so I was careful. I had 
several full healings, used a couple on pestilence himself and drank the 
others when ill. Pestilence fell to my +7 Grayswandir in two hits after 
the potions. I went on to find the High Altar of Loki... and I still had 
a magic lamp. Time for a helm of opposite alignment...

Done! I really wish I'd made a savegame and/or had the dump patch. Oh 
well. I feel kind of cheap using the helm to ascend but I figured for 
the first time nothing is off limits. Rodney only showed up 3 or 4 
times, I think, and I only got stuff cursed maybe thrice. I played a 
very careful game and genocided liberally (actually only bothered with 
L, ;, R, and the mind flayers). Every time a c showed up, I stopped and 
double checked everything, then killed with daggers at a distance. I 
never used Mjollnir even for throwing because of the explosion effect. I 
didn't even walk over a footrice I'm so afraid of them, and the only 
reason I didn't geno them is because I knew I wanted a corpse. Can you 
wish for a corpse even if they've been geno'd? I've lost MANY a 
promising character to footrice stupidity.

So... yeah. No printout for you. Hope you enjoyed my rambling.

